==English==

===Etymology===
From the act of tying or even nailing a pigeon to a stool to act as a decoy by hunters. Alternatively, from an alteration of {{com|en|stale|t1=decoy|pigeon}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-stool pigeon.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|originally}} A [[pigeon]] [[tied]] to a [[stool]] by a [[piece]] of [[twine]], used as a [[decoy]] to [[entice]] [[free-flying]] [[bird]]s to the [[ground]] to be [[shoot|shot]] or [[trap]]ped.
# {{lb|en|slang|obsolete|gambling}} A [[decoy]] used in a [[crooked]] [[gambling]] [[game]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} An [[informer]] to the [[authority|authorities]], especially one who [[give up|gives up]] [[criminal]] [[associate]]s.
#: {{syn|en|stoolie|stooly|Thesaurus:informant}}

